Instrument history, because the earlier captures of this file were wrong twice over.

1) The 05:11Z capture was taken mid-repair and records
   test-wave-integrity-adversarial.rkt red (1/8) while the W6 rehearsal matrix was still
   pinned to the superseded identity (fc1a6fa36 / a1b99fe2) before regeneration to
   50bdf7334 / fb224a6f. Review round 3 read that as contradicting release-preflight.json's
   0-failures claim, correctly.

2) The 21:53Z and 22:38Z re-runs used bare 'raco test'. That is the wrong instrument here:
   it exits 0 even when a case fails, AND for a file whose entry point is 'module+ main'
   rather than 'module+ test' it executes NOTHING and still exits 0. Two of the 19 files are
   shaped that way - test-deterministic-clock.rkt and
   test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt - so for those the green was vacuous: a pass that
   ran zero tests. The 21:53Z run also miscounted its own footer, matching rackunit's green
   '0 failure(s)' line as a failure and reporting 11 of 19. Review rounds 3 and 4 found both.

3) This run uses the project's own runner per file, which is the instrument whose exit code
   scripts/run-tests/reporting.rkt actually gates on (failed-result? is purely 'exit code
   neither 0 nor 2'). The per-file PASS/FAIL lines below come from that runner, and the
   footer counts those lines rather than grepping test output - the same lesson applied to
   the detector that was itself wrong twice.

The tracked-modification count is non-zero because this capture is being rewritten during
the commit that binds it. No test file is among the uncommitted changes, so these results
describe the merge candidate's code.

